    "introduction": "In order to switch the stitching styles of your sewing machine, the stitch select knob must be properly functioning. This guide will show the steps for replacement.",
    "what_you_need": {
        "tools": [
            {
                "text": "Phillips #2 Screwdriver",
                "url": "https://www.ifixit.com/products/6-in-1-screwdriver",
                "image": "https://cart-products.cdn.ifixit.com/cart-products/LYcK13TjejldWD5Y.thumbnail",
                "price": "$6.99"
            }
        ]
    },
    "steps": [
        {
            "step_number": 1,
            "title": "Back Panel",
            "text": "Place the machine on a solid surface.\nRemove the 14mm Phillips #2 screw holding on the face cover.",
            "image": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/xUpvdVUuBtCAINGw.medium",
            "image_links": [],
            "edit_link": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/22763/59538",
            "comment_links": []
        },
        {
            "step_number": 2,
            "title": "",
            "text": "Remove the two 14mm Phillips #2 screws and two 22mm Phillips #2 screws that secure the rear casing.",
            "image": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/htxYfpdJaFOwTnAd.medium",
            "image_links": [],
            "edit_link": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/22763/59516",
            "comment_links": []
        },
        {
            "step_number": 3,
            "title": "",
            "text": "Lay the machine on its side.\nRemove the four 10mm Phillips #2 screws that hold the bottom panel in place.\nThe feet will come off with the screws.",
            "image_links": [],
            "edit_link": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/22763/59520",
            "comment_links": []
        },
        {
            "step_number": 4,
            "title": "",
            "text": "Remove the bottom panel.",
            "image_links": [],
            "edit_link": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/22763/59537",
            "comment_links": []
        },
        {
            "step_number": 5,
            "title": "",
            "text": "Place the machine upright.\nRemove the rear casing.\nYou may have to wiggle the panel and pull at the same time.",
            "image_links": [],
            "edit_link": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/22763/59521",
            "comment_links": []
        },
        {
            "step_number": 6,
            "title": "Stitch Select Knob",
            "text": "Adjust the knob to gain access to the phillips head screw.",
            "image_links": [],
            "edit_link": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/22763/59610",
            "comment_links": []
        },
        {
            "step_number": 7,
            "title": "",
            "text": "Remove the 14mm Phillips #2 screw.",
            "image_links": [],
            "edit_link": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/22763/59611",
            "comment_links": []
        },
        {
            "step_number": 8,
            "title": "",
            "text": "Remove the knob.",
            "image_links": [],
            "edit_link": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/22763/59612",
            "comment_links": []
        }
    ],
    "conclusion": {
        "text": "To reassemble your device, follow these instructions in reverse order.",
